       EVP_PKEY-EC, EVP_KEYMGMT-EC - EVP_PKEY EC keytype and algorithm support

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The EECC keytype is implemented in OpenSSL’s default provider.

   CCoommmmoonn EECC ppaarraammeetteerrss
       The normal way of specifying domain parameters for an EC curve is via
       the curve name "group". For curves with no curve name, explicit
       parameters can be used that specify "field‐type", "p", "a", "b",
       "generator" and "order".  Explicit parameters are supported for
       backwards compatibility reasons, but they are not compliant with
       multiple standards (including RFC5915) which only allow named curves.

       The following KeyGen/Gettable/Import/Export types are available for the
       built‐in EC algorithm:

       "group" (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__GGRROOUUPP__NNAAMMEE) <UTF8 string>
           The curve name.

       "field‐type" (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__EECC__FFIIEELLDD__TTYYPPEE) <UTF8 string>
           The  value  should  be either "prime‐field" or "characteristic‐two‐
           field", which correspond to prime field Fp and binary field F2ˆm.

       "p" (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__EECC__PP) <unsigned integer>
           For a curve over Fp _p is the prime for the field. For a curve  over
           F2ˆm  _p represents the irreducible polynomial - each bit represents
           a term in the polynomial. Therefore, there will either be three  or
           five bits set dependent on whether the polynomial is a trinomial or
           a pentanomial.

       "a" (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__EECC__AA) <unsigned integer>
       "b" (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__EECC__BB) <unsigned integer>
       "seed" (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__EECC__SSEEEEDD) <octet string>
           _a  and _b represents the coefficients of the curve For Fp:   yˆ2 mod
           p = xˆ3 +ax + b mod p OR For F2ˆm: yˆ2 + xy = xˆ3 + axˆ2 + b

           _s_e_e_d is an optional value that is for  information  purposes  only.
           It   represents  the  random  number  seed  used  to  generate  the
           coefficient _b from a random number.

       "generator" (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__EECC__GGEENNEERRAATTOORR) <octet string>
       "order" (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__EECC__OORRDDEERR) <unsigned integer>
       "cofactor" (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__EECC__CCOOFFAACCTTOORR) <unsigned integer>
           The _g_e_n_e_r_a_t_o_r is a well defined  point  on  the  curve  chosen  for
           cryptographic  operations. The encoding conforms with Sec. 2.3.3 of
           the SECG  SEC  1  ("Elliptic  Curve  Cryptography")  standard.  See
           EECC__PPOOIINNTT__oocctt22ppooiinntt(()).  Integers used for point multiplications will
           be  between 0 and _o_r_d_e_r - 1.  _c_o_f_a_c_t_o_r is an optional value.  _o_r_d_e_r
           multiplied by the _c_o_f_a_c_t_o_r gives the number of points on the curve.

       "decoded‐from‐explicit"
       (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__EECC__DDEECCOODDEEDD__FFRROOMM__EEXXPPLLIICCIITT__PPAARRAAMMSS) <integer>
           Gets a flag indicating whether the key or parameters  were  decoded
           from  explicit  curve  parameters.  Set  to 1 if so or 0 if a named
           curve was used.

       "use‐cofactor‐flag" (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__UUSSEE__CCOOFFAACCTTOORR__EECCDDHH) <integer>
           Enable Cofactor DH (ECC CDH) if this value is 1, otherwise it  uses
           normal  EC DH if the value is zero. The cofactor variant multiplies
           the shared secret by the EC curve’s cofactor (note for some  curves
           the cofactor is 1).

           See      also      EEVVPP__KKEEYYEEXXCCHH--EECCDDHH(7)      for     the     related
           OOSSSSLL__EEXXCCHHAANNGGEE__PPAARRAAMM__EECC__EECCDDHH__CCOOFFAACCTTOORR__MMOODDEE parameter that can be set
           on a per‐operation basis.

       "encoding" (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__EECC__EENNCCOODDIINNGG) <UTF8 string>
           Set the format used for serializing the EC group parameters.  Valid
           values are  "explicit"  or  "named_curve".  The  default  value  is
           "named_curve".

       "point‐format" (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__EECC__PPOOIINNTT__CCOONNVVEERRSSIIOONN__FFOORRMMAATT) <UTF8
       string>
           Sets   or  gets  the  point_conversion_form  for  the  _k_e_y.  For  a
           description of point_conversion_forms please  see  EECC__PPOOIINNTT__nneeww(3).
           Valid  values are "uncompressed" or "compressed". The default value
           is "uncompressed".

       "group‐check" (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__EECC__GGRROOUUPP__CCHHEECCKK__TTYYPPEE) <UTF8 string>
           Sets   or   Gets   the   type   of   group    check    done    when
           EEVVPP__PPKKEEYY__ppaarraamm__cchheecckk(())  is  called.   Valid  values  are "default",
           "named" and "named‐nist".  The "named" type checks that the  domain
           parameters  match  the  inbuilt  curve  parameters, "named‐nist" is
           similar but also checks that the named curve is a nist curve.   The
           "default"  type  does  domain  parameter validation for the OpenSSL
           default provider, but is equivalent to "named‐nist" for the OpenSSL
           FIPS provider.

       "include‐public" (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__EECC__IINNCCLLUUDDEE__PPUUBBLLIICC) <integer>
           Setting this value to 0 indicates that the public key should not be
           included when encoding the private key. The default value of 1 will
           include the public key.

       "pub" (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__PPUUBB__KKEEYY) <octet string>
           The public key value in encoded EC point format conforming to  Sec.
           2.3.3  and  2.3.4 of the SECG SEC 1 ("Elliptic Curve Cryptography")
           standard.  This parameter is used when importing or  exporting  the
           public key value with the EEVVPP__PPKKEEYY__ffrroommddaattaa(()) and EEVVPP__PPKKEEYY__ttooddaattaa(())
           functions.

           Note,  in  particular,  that the choice of point compression format
           used for encoding the exported value via EEVVPP__PPKKEEYY__ttooddaattaa(())  depends
           on  the  underlying provider implementation.  Before OpenSSL 3.0.8,
           the implementation of providers included with OpenSSL always  opted
           for  an  encoding  in  compressed  format,  unconditionally.  Since
           OpenSSL 3.0.8, the implementation has been  changed  to  honor  the
           OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__EECC__PPOOIINNTT__CCOONNVVEERRSSIIOONN__FFOORRMMAATT parameter, if set, or to
           default to uncompressed format.

       "priv" (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__PPRRIIVV__KKEEYY) <unsigned integer>
           The private key value.

       "encoded‐pub‐key" (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__EENNCCOODDEEDD__PPUUBBLLIICC__KKEEYY) <octet string>
           Used  for getting and setting the encoding of an EC public key. The
           public key is expected to be a point conforming to  Sec.  2.3.4  of
           the SECG SEC 1 ("Elliptic Curve Cryptography") standard.

       "qx" (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__EECC__PPUUBB__XX) <unsigned integer>
           Used for getting the EC public key X component.

       "qy" (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__EECC__PPUUBB__YY) <unsigned integer>
           Used for getting the EC public key Y component.

       "default‐digest" (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__DDEEFFAAUULLTT__DDIIGGEESSTT) <UTF8 string>
           Getter  that  returns  the default digest name.  (Currently returns
           "SHA256" as of OpenSSL 3.0).

       The following Gettable types are also available  for  the  built‐in  EC
       algorithm:

       "basis‐type" (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__EECC__CCHHAARR22__TTYYPPEE) <UTF8 string>
